# Workspace rules — career-ops

Project rules for Windsurf/Devin (Cascade). Keep thin — durable project
knowledge lives in `memories/PROJECT_CONTEXT.md`.

## Before any work (do not skip)

1. Read `memories/PROJECT_CONTEXT.md` — canonical project state and the last
   session's handoff note (possibly written by Claude CLI, Codex CLI, Antigravity CLI, or
   Devin CLI; treat it as your own prior work).
   **If this file is missing or empty, this project is not onboarded.**
   Run the scaffold yourself in the integrated terminal (do not ask the user):
   - Windows: `& "$env:USERPROFILE\.local\bin\new-project-init.ps1" .`
   - macOS/Linux: `new-project-init .`
   Then invoke `/project-onboard` or ask Cascade to "onboard this project per
   the shared agent protocol" before any substantive work.
2. Read the header of `memories/graph-snapshot.md` for the dependency
   topology. If missing or stale, regenerate per
   `~/.agents/instructions/graphify.instructions.md`.
3. Follow the shared protocol: `~/.agents/AGENT_PROTOCOL.md`.

## Before you stop (mandatory — no mechanical enforcement in IDE)

YOU must enforce this yourself. Cascade will not remind you.

1. Update `memories/PROJECT_CONTEXT.md`:
   - Bump the "Last updated:" line.
   - Sprint Goal — still correct? Edit or delete.
   - Decisions Log — append any new decisions with WHY.
   - Pitfalls — append anything that burned this session.
   - Open Tasks — check off completed, add new, delete stale.
2. Rewrite the **Last Session Handoff Note** (Section 7) from scratch:
   - **From:** this tool / **To:** any
   - **When:** today's date
   - **Task:** one-line summary of what this session did
   - **Current files:** any files still in progress
   - **Last changes:** files touched and what changed
   - **Graph snapshot:** refreshed? (yes/no + commit)
   - **Verified:** what was checked (tests, lint, build)
   - **Unresolved questions:** anything blocking or unclear
   - **Next immediate action:** what the next agent should do first
3. If the architecture changed, refresh `memories/graph-snapshot.md` first.
4. Mirror any Cascade Memory you created into `memories/PROJECT_CONTEXT.md`.
   Other tools cannot read Cascade Memories. File-based memory wins on conflict.

## Project specifics

- Build/test: root CI gate is `node test-all.mjs --quick`; dashboard package tests are `npm --prefix apps/job-dashboard test`; tracker health is `node verify-pipeline.mjs`.
- Local dashboard: start from `apps/job-dashboard/scripts/start-local.ps1`; server is `127.0.0.1:3000`, runner control is `127.0.0.1:48731`.
- Data contract: user layer (`cv.md`, `config/profile.yml`, `modes/_profile.md`, `portals.yml`, `data/*`, `reports/*`, `output/*`) is personal; never move personalization into system files.
- Tracker rule: add new evaluations via TSV in `batch/tracker-additions/` and `node merge-tracker.mjs`; edit `data/applications.md` only for existing rows.
- Current active work: fix `memories/session/review.md` Reviewer FAIL findings before new dashboard features.
